  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, leveraging AI, IoT, and Web3. It was introduced with a kick-off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, with an initial phase one budget of $500,000. The project team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). A call for ideas was issued in July, focusing on AI-enhanced data visualization. The executive board later approved a total budget of $2 million covering research, development, and marketing. Additional budgets were allocated for compliance ($55,000) and training ($15,000). Recent updates highlight a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, with a detailed report scheduled for November 20th. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, and partnership discussions with TechInnovate are underway."
